Restaurant Order Manager
Java Collections Assignment — ArrayList, LinkedList, HashMap & LinkedHashMap
1. Assignment Goal
Build a console-based Restaurant Order Management System. The main goal is to practice choosing and
using the appropriate Java collection for different types of data. The project should use ArrayList, LinkedList,
HashMap, and LinkedHashMap for clearly different responsibilities.
2. Learning Objectives
• Use ArrayList to store and manage the restaurant menu.
• Use LinkedList to represent the kitchen order queue.
• Use HashMap to find any order quickly using its order ID, regardless of its current status.
• Use LinkedHashMap to keep completed orders in their completion order.
• Work with custom objects inside Java collections.
• Practice adding, removing, searching, and displaying collection data.
• Understand why one collection may be more suitable than another for a specific task.
• Use an enum to represent and control the current status of an order.
