5. Operation Requirements
Add Menu Item
Read the item's ID, name, price, and category. Add it to the ArrayList menu. Menu item IDs must be unique.
Remove Menu Item
Remove a menu item using its ID. If the item does not exist, display an appropriate message.
Display Menu
Display all menu items stored in the ArrayList.
Search Menu Item
Search for a menu item by ID and display it if found.
Create Order
Read an order ID and customer name. The order ID must be unique. The new order starts with PENDING
status and is stored in the HashMap. The order remains in the HashMap for its entire lifecycle.
Add Item to Order
Find the order by ID, find the requested menu item by ID, read the quantity, and add an OrderItem to the
order. Items should not be added to orders that are already COMPLETED or CANCELLED.
Remove Item from Order
Find the order and remove the requested item from that order. Items should not be modified after the order
is COMPLETED or CANCELLED.
Display Order
Display the customer, order ID, status, all ordered items, quantities, subtotals, and the final total.Add Order to Kitchen Queue
Find the order using the HashMap and add it to the LinkedList kitchen queue. Change its status from
PENDING to IN_KITCHEN. An order should not be added to the queue more than once.
Process Next Order
Process the first order in the kitchen queue. Use the LinkedList as a queue, change its status to
COMPLETED, and add it to the LinkedHashMap of completed orders. Keep the same order in the
HashMap.
Search Order
Search for any order by its ID using the HashMap, regardless of whether it is PENDING, IN_KITCHEN,
COMPLETED, or CANCELLED.
Check Order Status
Ask the user for an order ID, find the order using the HashMap, and display its current OrderStatus.
Display Completed Orders
Display all completed orders in the same order in which they were completed. The LinkedHashMap should
preserve this order.
6. Order Lifecycle
The order moves through the system while remaining in the HashMap:
Create Order → PENDING
Add Order to Kitchen Queue → IN_KITCHEN
Process Next Order → COMPLETED
Cancel Order (if implemented) → CANCELLED
The HashMap contains the order in every state. The kitchenQueue only contains orders waiting to be
processed, and completedOrders contains completed orders in completion order.
